Statically linked binaries bundled in the native package (agent-fleet-native-*,
docs/log/35 §35.7.2). Each is built unmodified from the upstream release tarball at
the version pinned in deploy/release/native/Dockerfile.tools:

  bubblewrap (bin/bwrap) — LGPL-2.0-or-later
    (https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap)
  git (bin/git, bin/git-http-backend) — GPL-2.0
    (https://git-scm.com; source: https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/)
  zstd (bin/zstd) — dual BSD-3-Clause / GPL-2.0, used under BSD-3-Clause
    (https://github.com/facebook/zstd)
  musl libc (statically linked into the above) — MIT License (https://musl.libc.org)
  libcap (statically linked into bwrap) — dual BSD-3-Clause / GPL-2.0
    (https://sites.google.com/site/fullycapable/)
  zlib (statically linked into git) — zlib License (https://zlib.net)

Fonts installed on demand by the native lean rootfs (install-chromium):
  Noto Sans CJK — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk)

Source code availability: components licensed under the GPL/LGPL family are
unmodified Debian packages; their corresponding sources are available from the
Debian archive (https://www.debian.org / `apt-get source <pkg>` against the
bookworm suite recorded in the image). The statically linked git and bubblewrap
binaries in the native package are built unmodified from the upstream release
tarballs at the exact versions pinned in deploy/release/native/Dockerfile.tools
(those tarballs are the corresponding source). On written request to the
distributor we will provide the corresponding source for any GPL/LGPL component
bundled in a distributed image or package.
